{"name":"Schist","hex":"#87876f","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"schist","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of a variety of coarse-grained crystalline metamorphic rocks with a foliated structure that allows easy division into slabs or slates."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/schist"}],"entries":[{"title":"Schist","blocks":[{"text":"Schist is a medium-grained metamorphic rock generally derived from fine-grained sedimentary rock, like shale. It shows pronounced schistosity. This means that the rock is composed of mineral grains easily seen with a low-power hand lens, oriented in such a way that the rock is easily split into thin flakes or plates. This texture reflects a high content of platy minerals, such as mica, talc, chlorite, or graphite. These are often interleaved with more granular minerals, such as feldspar or quartz."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6f/Schist_detail.jpg/330px-Schist_detail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Schist"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/Thin_section_of_garnet-mica-schist.jpg/250px-Thin_section_of_garnet-mica-schist.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/Thin_section_of_garnet-mica-schist.jpg/500px-Thin_section_of_garnet-mica-schist.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/Thin_section_of_garnet-mica-schist.jpg/250px-Thin_section_of_garnet-mica-schist.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThin_section_of_garnet-mica-schist.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/75/Normal_View_of_Garnet-Mica-Schist.JPG/250px-No